{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:97d4be8960698f97","name":"Conditions","source":{"id":"source:reference-97d4be8960698f97","title":"Conditions","revision":24990,"timestamp":"2024-11-10T16:50:31Z","sha256":"1204e88ef3d473888c9815a1d123bd8087e323c969c5cf072edf1fa36c465efe","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24990","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Conditions&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-97d4be8960698f97","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Certain debilitating attacks reduce one's combat effectiveness instead of one's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},". Examples include a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Stun Grenade"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stun_Grenade","referenceId":"reference:a6f6ca26ba3cde3c"}," blast, a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Forced March"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Forced_March"},", a paralyzing venom, or long-term exposure to extreme temperatures. Multiple Conditions have cumulative effects and can render a creature ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unconscious"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unconscious"},", or a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"},", or object ",{"tag":"a","children":["Disabled"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disabled"},". Physically debilitating attacks are usually made against the target's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},", while mentally deliberating attacks target one's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},". Either type of attack pushes the target along the same track.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Damage Threshold"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Attacks that deal massive amounts of damage can impair or incapacitate you regardless of how many ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"}," you have remaining. Your Damage Threshold determines how much ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage"}," a single attack must deal to reduce your combat effectiveness or, in some cases, kill you. When a single attack made against you deals damage that equals or exceeds your Damage Threshold, but not enough to drop you to 0 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},", you move -1 step along the Condition Track. If the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage"}," reduces you to 0 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},", you are dead (see ",{"tag":"a","children":["Death"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Death"},").\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Character Combat"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Damage Threshold = ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"}," + Size Modifier"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Size Modifier:"]}," Creatures, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," larger than Medium Size gain a Size bonus to their Damage Threshold. This Size bonus is:\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["+5 for Large,"]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["+10 for Huge,"]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["+20 for Gargantuan,"]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["and +50 for Colossal."]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Improved Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Improved_Damage_Threshold","referenceId":"reference:ccb956326c7947a0"},":"]}," You can increase your Damage Threshold by taking the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Improved Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Improved_Damage_Threshold","referenceId":"reference:ccb956326c7947a0"}," feat."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Vehicle Combat"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Damage Threshold = ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"}," + Size Modifier"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Size Modifier:"]}," Apply the following Size Modifiers to a Vehicle's Damage Threshold:\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["Large, +5;"]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["Huge, +10;"]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["Gargantuan, +20;"]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["Colossal, +50;"]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["Colossal (Frigate), +100;"]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["Colossal (Cruiser), +200;"]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["Colossal (Station), +500."]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Mass Combat"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Damage Threshold = ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"}," + 50 (Size Modifier)"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Improved Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Improved_Damage_Threshold","referenceId":"reference:ccb956326c7947a0"},":"]}," A Battalion can increase their Damage Threshold with the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Improved Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Improved_Damage_Threshold","referenceId":"reference:ccb956326c7947a0"}," feat."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["If a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalion"}," takes damage from a single attack that equals or exceeds its Damage Threshold, the Battalion moves -1 Persistent step down the Condition Track. This represents the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalion"}," taking a staggering blow that greatly reduces its efficiency. A ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalion"}," pushed to the bottom of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition_Track"}," must ",{"tag":"a","children":["Disband"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disband"}," on its next turn as its only Action.\n"]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["The Condition Track"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["A creature, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"},", object, or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," not affected by any debilitating Conditions is assumed to be in a \"Normal State,\" which represents one end of the Condition Track. Each debilitating effect to which it succumbs moves it one or more steps along the Condition Track. A creature pushed to the last step on the Condition Tack falls ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unconscious"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unconscious"},". A ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"},", or object pushed to the last step on the Condition Track is ",{"tag":"a","children":["Disabled"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disabled"}," until repaired using the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," skill. When a device is pushed down the Condition Track, apply the indicated penalty on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Checks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Checks"}," made with the device.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," is pushed down the Condition Track, all of the Vehicle's occupants suffer the same penalties as the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," itself until the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," is either Disabled or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Repaired"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Repaired"},". Penalties imposed by multiple Condition Tracks are cumulative; in other words, a Vehicle's occupants suffer the effects of their own personal Condition Tracks in addition to the effects of the Vehicle's Condition Track.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Jedi Counseling"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Counseling"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Counseling"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Q:"]}," Condition Track penalties reduce all your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Defense Scores"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Defense_Scores"},". Do they also reduce your Damage Threshold, since it is derived from your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},"?\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["A:"]}," Yes. Although the effect is indirect, any modifiers that change your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"}," also change your Damage Threshold by an equal amount because its underlying \"starting value\" has changed.\n"]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"caption","children":["THE CONDITION TRACK\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["Normal State (No Penalties)\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["-1 Step ↕ +1 Step\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["-1 Penalty to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Defenses"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Defenses","referenceId":"reference:0d85b79fde210d9c"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Attacks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attacks","referenceId":"reference:1e3a955bd202b306"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ability Checks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ability_Checks"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Checks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Checks"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["-1 Step ↕ +1 Step\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["-2 Penalty to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Defenses"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Defenses","referenceId":"reference:0d85b79fde210d9c"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Attacks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attacks","referenceId":"reference:1e3a955bd202b306"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ability Checks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ability_Checks"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Checks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Checks"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["-1 Step ↕ +1 Step\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["-5 Penalty to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Defenses"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Defenses","referenceId":"reference:0d85b79fde210d9c"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Attacks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attacks","referenceId":"reference:1e3a955bd202b306"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ability Checks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ability_Checks"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Checks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Checks"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["-1 Step ↕ +1 Step\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["Move at Half Speed; -10 Penalty to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Defenses"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Defenses","referenceId":"reference:0d85b79fde210d9c"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Attacks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attacks","referenceId":"reference:1e3a955bd202b306"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ability Checks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ability_Checks"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Checks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Checks"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["-1 Step ↕ +1 Step\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Helpless"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Helpless"}," (Unconscious or Disabled)\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Removing Conditions"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["You can improve your Condition by spending three ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Actions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Actions"}," to use the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Recover"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Recover","referenceId":"reference:0c5327fd45c72552"}," Action, moving +1 step along the Condition Track. You can spend all Three ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Actions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Actions"}," in a single round, or spread them out across consecutive rounds.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["For example, you could spend a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"}," at the end of one turn and two ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Actions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Actions"}," at the start of your next turn to move +1 step along the Condition Track. Certain situations, such as Persistent Conditions, may prevent you from spending ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Actions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Actions"}," to move toward a Normal State on the Condition Track.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Resting for eight consecutive, uninterrupted hours usually removes all debilitating Conditions afflicting a creature and returns it to its Normal State. However, some Persistent Conditions, such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Poison"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Poison"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hunger"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hunger?action=edit&redlink=1"},", may prevent a creature from improving its Condition or returning to its Normal State until the cause of the debilitation is treated.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Battalion Conditions"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["When a Battalion is moved down the Condition Track by attacks that equal or exceed its Damage Threshold, its movement down the Condition Track is always a Persistent Condition (this represents the Battalion taking a staggering blow that greatly reduces its efficiency). A Battalion pushed to the bottom of the Condition Track must ",{"tag":"a","children":["Disband"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disband"}," on its next turn as its only Action. \n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Persistent Conditions"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Some ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hazards"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hazards"}," and attacks result in a Persistent Condition that cannot be removed except in certain circumstances. Any time a Condition is Persistent, you cannot use the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Recover"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Recover","referenceId":"reference:0c5327fd45c72552"}," Action to move steps up the Condition Track, and you do not regain any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"}," from ",{"tag":"a","children":["Natural Healing"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Natural_Healing"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["However, once a Persistent Condition is removed by satisfying the requirements starting in its description, you can move up the Condition Track and heal normally.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Persistent Conditions do not prevent you from moving up the Condition Track by means other than the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Recover"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Recover","referenceId":"reference:0c5327fd45c72552"}," Action or resting for eight hours. For example, an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unconscious"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unconscious"}," creature that fails its first ",{"tag":"a","children":["Constitution"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Constitution"}," check has a Persistent Condition from its injuries, but it still moves +1 step on the Condition Track when it makes a successful ",{"tag":"a","children":["Constitution"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Constitution"}," check to regain consciousness.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Multiple Persistent Conditions"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Sometimes you are affected by more than one Persistent Condition. For example, you might be ",{"tag":"a","children":["Poisoned"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Poisoned"}," after already suffering the effects of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Disease"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disease"},". In this case, you must satisfy the requirements for removing all these Persistent Conditions before you can move up the Condition Track.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
